# Silhouette (CR 615.1, 120.2a-b, 701.14a): "If a spell or ability that targets that creature would cause a source to deal damage
# to that creature this turn, prevent that damage" prevents only damage dealt to that creature, and none that is no spell's or
# ability's. On turn 3 Bot1 casts Silhouette on its Grizzled Leotau (1/5), then Plow Through has the Leotau fight Bot2's Hill
# Giant (3/3): the Giant's 3 damage to the Leotau, which Plow Through targets, is prevented; the Leotau's 1 to the Giant is dealt.
# Then the Leotau attacks and the Giant blocks: combat damage is caused by no spell or ability, so the Giant's 3 is dealt to the
# Leotau, and the Giant has 2 in all.

